# Local reference copies of earlier versions of the app. Imported by nothing,
# never bundled. App_broadsheet.jsx has a hardcoded GM password on line 8 from
# before auth moved server-side into api/gm.js — these stay out of the repo.
src/App_old.jsx
src/App_broadsheet.jsx

# The generated roster: thirty live three-word codes, and a code IS the player
# who holds it. The whole security model rests on codes never being fetchable —
# `players` has no anon SELECT policy for exactly this reason — so committing
# them would just move the credential behind a different lock, and git history
# is forever. Nothing reads this file at runtime: it is generated by
# scripts/generate-players.mjs, pasted into the SQL editor once, and after that
# the database is the source of truth (GM panel → Players → Copy roster CSV).
supabase/players.seed.sql
